  "notes": "Emo-pop with a soul-derived vocal: 80–151 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 and the signature singles at 117–137. The fact that shapes this model most is a tracking-order one — the kit went down \"**first, before bass**\", and the bass was then \"fitted around the already-recorded rhythm guitar… tuned against the guitars rather than the kick\". That is why the bassline is `independent_riff` at 0.8 with root-and-octave motion instead of the kick-lock every other band in this bench gets. Three drum deltas are quoted: \"kick 1 and the '&' of 3\", \"snare 2&4 with a bright crack\" (a loud accent over a tight main), and \"16th tom fills into choruses\", which is the tom-led perc block on a 4-bar schedule; heavy pre-production means the parts are fixed before tracking, hence the tight grid. Harmony is minor-leaning verses opening into major choruses — i–VI–III–VII into I–V–vi–IV — with a suspended pre-chorus. The melody is the entry's other distinctive claim: \"R&B-inflected — melismatic runs and a wide range over punk chords\", so the density runs 5–11 across a two-octave register with a raised third share, and the \"hooks often placed in the pre-chorus rather than the chorus\" is why the pre-chorus is as long as the chorus in `sectionBars`. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium and marks the harmonic claims **[LOW-CONF]**, which is why `keys` is left inherited. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every drum probability and `bpm.mode` 127.",
